<task id="205e" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration — row A43 (Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1 silent-fallback gate — §10.5 trap 2)</title>
    <phase>Phase Pre-Live-Fire — Auth-v4 runtime-contract integration (task 205)</phase>
    <gate>ready</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Per project CLAUDE.md rigor table + root CLAUDE.md §8 TEST-MODIFYING/auth override: A43 gates a silent-fallback path that (if left ungated) quietly re-mints an AI Search admin key on secret-free envs — a §10.5 trap-2 silent-Δ2-reversal vector directly attacking the auth-v4 secret-free credential contract (`AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true`). Row is tagged `auth` (secret-management surface), which triggers unconditional code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5 per root CLAUDE.md §8 override; ADR-028 A4 rationale (secret-free BFF identity — per `notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` APPROVED 2026-08-25) must be preserved by this gate.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical apply of a well-specified delta per remediation plan §5.3 bullet 3.2 and punch row A43: (a) add gate condition (KV tag OR `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true`) BEFORE the existing silent fallback at `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:340-366`, (b) branch to FAIL LOUD or AAD-token path per gate outcome, (c) preserve current fallback for pre-migration envs. PowerShell-only under `scripts/ai-search/**`; disjoint file surface from A38/A39/A41/A42/A44. Precedent already exists inline at `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:617-660` (`-CutoverBffSettings` MI-check refusal pattern) — this row extends that shape to the general resolution path. No credential logic authoring, no cross-worktree consumption; scoped mechanical change per §8.5 Sonnet-5 default.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>PowerShell-only under `scripts/ai-search/**` (single file `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` + any new tests). Disjoint from A38 (`Handlers/KvSecretsPopulation/**` manifests), A42 (`H3EntraAppRegHandler`), A39 (`H4bBulkAppSettingsHandler` manifest), A41 (H10 + T2 probe + `design.md`), A44 (`appsettings.template.json` consumer guard + doc sweep). Sonnet @ high; can run parallel with A38/A42/A44 as a low-priority background agent per remediation plan §7 (A43 lives in the "S2 → A35 → A43/A44 pre-Phase-F-not-pre-186" lane).</parallel-reason>
    <deps>A35 (landed)</deps>
    <tags>provisioning, auth, powershell, ai-search, silent-fallback-gate</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2h (per punch row A43 landing spot `scripts/ai-search`, effort-h 2)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Apply punch row **A43** from `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` A-blocks-E2E MAYBE/NO table: gate `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1`'s silent admin-key fallback (currently `:349` "KV secret 'AiSearch--AdminKey' not found in $KeyVaultName — falling back to live admin key from search service." followed by `az search admin-key show` at `:357-360`) so that on secret-free envs (marker present OR `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true`) the script NEVER re-mints the admin key — because a silent re-mint quietly reverses the auth-v4 Δ2 migration while the run reports green (§10.5 trap 2; §5.3 bullet 3.2 of the remediation plan). Row-shape (per row A43): (a) grep-verify current state at `:340-366` BEFORE editing; (b) apply the three-branch gate — (1) if secret-free marker present + secret missing → FAIL LOUD with actionable message linking to the A38 omit contract, (2) if `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true` → use AAD-token path (`Get-AzAccessToken -ResourceUrl "https://search.azure.com/"`), (3) if neither → keep current fallback (backwards compat for pre-migration envs); (c) preserve script idempotency (re-run safe); (d) add unit-test coverage for MI-enabled + secret-free-marker branches; (e) integration-verify against a secret-free env (no admin key minted) AND a pre-migration env (current behavior preserved); (f) amend punch-list annotation `last_known_status_after_execution`. Model 1 shared-KV vs Model 2 per-customer `kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer}` × N vaults: the gate MUST work identically across N vaults per §10.1 Δ2 + §10.3 (a missed marker on one vault is itself a silent-skip failure — see A38 fleet-consistency note). Precedent to extend: `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:617-660` `-CutoverBffSettings` already implements the shape of this gate (queries `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled` via `az webapp config appsettings list` and refuses on `true`); mirror that pattern into the general resolution path at `:340-366`. Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</prompt>

  <role>PowerShell hardening specialist + AI Search authentication expert + auth-v4 credential-contract preserver. Expert in: (a) the Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1 canonical-catalog authority (per project CLAUDE.md pattern table — "the script IS the catalog authority"); (b) the auth-v4 secret-free credential contract per master ADR-028 A4 (verified via A35 merge) — MI-FIC default, KV cert fallback, NEVER `.WithClientSecret(...)` for BFF identity; (c) the §10.5 silent-fallback trap-class (admin-key re-mint = Δ2 reversal disguised as green run) and the analogous `-CutoverBffSettings` mitigation already present inline at `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:617-660`; (d) the Azure AI Search AAD-token pattern (`Get-AzAccessToken -ResourceUrl "https://search.azure.com/"`) as the MI-enabled replacement for the admin-key REST auth path; (e) KV-tag vs env-config gate ordering per A38's secret-free-marker contract (marker on the KV, not in the credential slot — §9.1); (f) fleet-consistency invariants under Model 2 per-customer vaults (§10.3).</role>

  <goal>Row A43 annotated with `last_known_status_after_execution` in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md`. `scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` gates its silent admin-key fallback (currently at `:340-366`) on a three-branch decision: (1) secret-free marker present (KV tag on the vault, per A38 omit contract) AND `AiSearch--AdminKey` secret missing → **FAIL LOUD** with actionable message that names the marker, links to the A38 omit contract (constraint file location + row number), and refuses to mint an admin key; (2) `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true` in the BFF app-settings → use AAD-token path via `Get-AzAccessToken -ResourceUrl "https://search.azure.com/"` (no admin key resolved at all; REST calls in the script switch to `Authorization: Bearer` header); (3) neither marker nor MI flag → keep current `az search admin-key show` fallback UNCHANGED (backwards compat for pre-migration envs). Silent admin-key re-mint path REMOVED for secret-free envs (grep-verify: after edit, `az search admin-key show` cannot execute when secret-free marker present). FAIL-LOUD message actionable + links to A38 omit contract (constraint file path + row number). AAD-token path exercised in a unit test (MI-enabled env → token acquired + REST call uses Bearer header). Backwards compat preserved: a pre-migration env (no marker + no MI flag) → current fallback behavior unchanged (unit-test coverage). Script idempotency preserved: re-runs against a secret-free env produce identical no-op behavior (integration test asserts no side effects on repeated run). Model 1 and Model 2 fleet-consistency: gate MUST work identically across N per-customer vaults; documented in the gate's inline comment block. `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` still parses + executes cleanly (`pwsh -NoProfile -Command "& { . '.\scripts\ai-search\Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1' -WhatIf ... }"` or equivalent syntax check succeeds). Zero regression of the existing `-CutoverBffSettings` gate at `:617-660` (that path already implements the same shape; new gate lives ABOVE it in the general resolution path).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Punch row A43 ("trap2-deploy-allindexes-gate") is a §10.5 trap-2 quality gate — pre-Phase-F, not a pre-186 hard-blocker per punch list A-blocks-E2E MAYBE/NO table, but strongly recommended before live-fire because every re-deploy or rotation of the AI Search index catalog quietly reverses the auth-v4 Δ2 migration if the gate is absent. The current script at `scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:340-366` executes `az search admin-key show --service-name ... --query primaryKey -o tsv` whenever the KV secret `AiSearch--AdminKey` is absent — a fallback that, on secret-free envs where the secret was DELETED as part of the auth-v4 migration (see remediation plan §5.3 bullet 3.2), silently re-issues an admin key and reports green while runtime silently uses the admin-key path. This is the same trap-class as the `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:617-660` `-CutoverBffSettings` mitigation already applied inline (which checks `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true` and refuses to cutover) — A43 extends that shape to the general resolution path. Detection surface: (a) KV tag on the customer vault (secret-free marker per A38 omit contract, §9.1 — "positive migration marker = KV tag or provisioning-state field, never the credential slot"); (b) BFF app-setting `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true` (per §10.2 live contract — one of the 8 credential-selection settings A39 will provision). Under Model 2, N per-customer `kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer}` vaults each carry their own marker; the gate MUST NOT assume Model 1 shared-KV shape (§10.3 fleet-consistency). A43 depends on A35 (landed) because the ADR-028 A4 amendment governing "why this gate exists" arrived via the master merge — pre-A35 this worktree's ADR-028 had no A4 (verified via commits `dee3df03c` / `39b2bda38` not being HEAD ancestors before A35). A43 does NOT depend on A38 being fully authored — the KV-tag marker scheme A38 defines is the PRIMARY gate signal, but the env-config `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true` gate is a SECONDARY/independent signal; if A38's tag scheme is still in-flight at execution time, A43 uses env-config as the primary gate and adds a tag-check placeholder that A38 completes.</background>
