      <dependency task="A38" status="parallel-safe">A38 defines the KV-tag secret-free-marker scheme. A43 uses env-config `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true` as the PRIMARY gate (independent signal) AND KV-tag as SECONDARY. If A38 tag scheme is still in-flight, A43 lands with a tag-check placeholder + explicit `# TODO(A38): finalize tag key/value` comment; A38 executor closes the placeholder at its landing time.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="punch row A43 (auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md)">MUST gate the silent fallback on secret-free marker OR `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true`; MUST NOT re-mint admin key on secret-free envs (silent Δ2 reversal); MUST use AAD-token path when `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true`; FAIL-LOUD message MUST link to A38 omit contract for actionable operator guidance; backwards compat: pre-migration envs (no marker + no MI flag) MUST keep current fallback behavior; MUST NOT regress Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1 idempotency (script re-runs must be safe).</constraint>
    <constraint source="remediation plan §5.3 bullet 3.2">Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1 silent admin-key fallback is a confirmed live migration-undo vector; gate MUST be applied on the machine-readable secret-free marker (KV tag or provisioning-state field — NEVER a value in the credential slot per §9.1).</constraint>
    <constraint source="§10.5 trap 2">The gate MUST NEVER silently re-mint the admin key on secret-free envs. FAIL LOUD is the ONLY correct behavior when the marker says secret-free but the secret is missing. `az search admin-key show` MUST NOT execute in that branch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§10.3 (fleet consistency, Model 2)">Under Model 2, N per-customer `kv-{customerId}-{secretsVer}` vaults each carry their own marker. Gate MUST work identically across N vaults; MUST NOT assume Model 1 shared-KV shape. Document in an inline comment block.</constraint>
    <constraint source="§9.1 (marker location, BINDING)">Positive migration marker = KV tag OR provisioning-state field, NEVER a sentinel value in the credential slot (sentinels produce opaque `AADSTS7000215`). A43 gate MUST read the marker from a KV tag OR from env-config, not from the secret value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 A4 (per master merge A35)">MUST NOT call `.WithClientSecret(...)` for any client authenticating as the BFF identity — the gate MUST NOT introduce any secret-authenticated code path when MI is enabled. AAD-token path is the ONLY correct MI-enabled resolution.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §3 Sub-Agent Write Boundary">A43 does NOT touch `.claude/**` — sub-agent write boundary N/A. But `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` annotation edit is main-session-safe (project notes are not `.claude/`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="root CLAUDE.md §11 component justification">The gate is an EXTENSION of the existing `-CutoverBffSettings` mitigation (`:617-660`) — not a new component. If a new tests file is created, MUST cite punch row A43 in file header + answer Existing/Extension/Cost-of-doing-nothing per §11.</constraint>
    <constraint source="script IS the catalog authority (project CLAUDE.md canonical implementations)">Do NOT introduce a competing catalog file; keep the gate + catalog authoring inline in Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1 per the established pattern.</constraint>
    <constraint source="pattern precedent (Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:617-660)">Existing `-CutoverBffSettings` gate queries `az webapp config appsettings list --query "[?name=='AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled'].value | [0]" -o tsv 2>$null` — mirror this exact query shape for consistency; do NOT invent a divergent query.</constraint>
    <constraint source="A38 forward-compat">If A38's KV-tag marker scheme is finalized before A43 lands, use A38's canonical tag key/value; if not, add explicit `# TODO(A38): finalize tag key/value` placeholder — do NOT invent a divergent scheme.</constraint>
  </constraints>

