  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL block (FULL, high effort, sonnet tier). Read `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` rows A38 + A43 + A44 (context for trap-2 gate + A38 omit contract linkage). Read `notes/auth-v4-integration-remediation-plan.md` §5 priority surfaces bullet 3 (migration-undo vectors) + §7 sequencing (A43 lane) + §8 effort. Read `notes/decisions/adr-028-a4-integration-conflict-resolution.md` §"Owner refinements 2026-08-25" + rationale (why the gate matters). Read `.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md` A4 + E-3 CLOSED banner (post-A35 merge). Read `scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` in full (esp. `:340-366` current fallback + `:617-660` `-CutoverBffSettings` precedent).</step>
    <step order="1" name="Grep-verify current state BEFORE editing">Run grep for `az search admin-key show`, `AiSearch--AdminKey`, `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled`, `Get-AzAccessToken`, `search.azure.com` in `scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1`. Confirm: (a) silent fallback still at `:340-366` (matches punch list source-of-truth); (b) `-CutoverBffSettings` MI-check at `:617-660` still present (precedent to extend); (c) `Get-AzAccessToken` NOT already present (would indicate a prior partial fix — reconcile if found). Record verified state in scratchpad table.</step>
    <step order="2" name="Verify A38 tag-scheme status">Read `.claude/constraints/auth.md` + `.claude/constraints/provisioning.md` + `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` A38 landing status. If A38's KV-tag key/value is finalized, capture the canonical values. If not, plan to land the gate with `# TODO(A38): finalize tag key/value` placeholder + reference to punch row A38 in comment.</step>
    <step order="3" name="Verify Az.Accounts / Get-AzAccessToken support">Run `Get-Command Get-AzAccessToken -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object -Property Name, Source, Version` to confirm the `Az.Accounts` module is available in the pwsh environment. If not, capture the fallback (invoke `az account get-access-token --resource https://search.azure.com/ --query accessToken -o tsv` via the `az` CLI). Escalation trigger fires if NEITHER path is supported.</step>
    <step order="4" name="Checkpoint (after load + verification)">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "✅ Checkpoint.").</step>
    <step order="5" name="Apply A43 gate — three-branch decision at Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:340-366">EDIT `scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` to insert the gate BEFORE the current silent fallback. Structure: (a) FIRST resolve gate signals: (1) `$secretFreeMarker` = `az keyvault show --name $KeyVaultName --query "tags.<CANONICAL_TAG_KEY_FROM_A38_OR_TODO>" -o tsv 2>$null` (returns marker value or empty); (2) `$miEnabled` = `az webapp config appsettings list --name $BffAppName --resource-group $BffResourceGroup --query "[?name=='AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled'].value | [0]" -o tsv 2>$null` (mirror `:631` query shape). (b) Branch 1 (secret-free marker present + secret missing): `Write-Error` with FAIL-LOUD message naming the marker + linking to A38 omit contract (`.claude/constraints/auth.md` + row A38 in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md`); `exit 6` (new exit code, distinct from existing exit 5 for admin-key-resolution failure). (c) Branch 2 (`$miEnabled -eq 'true'`): acquire AAD token via `Get-AzAccessToken -ResourceUrl "https://search.azure.com/"` (or `az account get-access-token --resource https://search.azure.com/ --query accessToken -o tsv` fallback if Az.Accounts unavailable); switch `$restHeaders` at `:369-372` from `'api-key' = $adminKey` to `'Authorization' = "Bearer $token"`; set a `$script:UsingAadAuth = $true` flag for later branching. (d) Branch 3 (neither marker nor MI flag): fall through to current behavior UNCHANGED (backwards compat). Add an inline comment block above the gate documenting: §10.5 trap 2 rationale, three-branch decision, Model 1 vs Model 2 fleet-consistency note, A38 forward-compat placeholder (if applicable), and the `:617-660` `-CutoverBffSettings` precedent this gate mirrors.</step>
    <step order="6" name="Verify no regression of :617-660 -CutoverBffSettings gate">Re-read `:617-660` after Step 5 edits to confirm the existing gate is untouched. Both gates coexist by design: A43 (this row) covers the GENERAL admin-key resolution path (every script invocation); `:617-660` covers the SPECIFIC `-CutoverBffSettings` operator action. They MUST NOT be merged — different failure surfaces.</step>
    <step order="7" name="Checkpoint (after gate applied)">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "✅ Checkpoint.").</step>
    <step order="8" name="Add unit + integration test coverage">Locate existing test surface for `scripts/ai-search/` (Pester or equivalent under `tests/` per project CLAUDE.md constraints/testing.md). Add tests: (a) UNIT — MI-enabled env → gate branch 2 fires → AAD token acquired → `$restHeaders` contains `Authorization` key (not `api-key`) → no `az search admin-key show` call; (b) UNIT — secret-free marker present + secret missing → gate branch 1 fires → `Write-Error` invoked + exit 6 → no admin-key mint; (c) UNIT — no marker + no MI flag → gate branch 3 fires → current fallback runs unchanged; (d) INTEGRATION — script re-run against a mocked secret-free env asserts zero admin-key mints across N repeated runs (idempotency); (e) INTEGRATION — script run against a mocked pre-migration env asserts current behavior byte-identical to pre-edit baseline. If no existing PowerShell test surface, create `tests/scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.Tests.ps1` with header citing punch row A43 + §11 justification (Existing / Extension / Cost-of-doing-nothing).</step>
    <step order="9" name="Syntax + smoke check">Run `pwsh -NoProfile -Command "& { Get-Command -Syntax '.\scripts\ai-search\Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1' }"` (or equivalent parse-check) to confirm script parses cleanly. Run the tests from Step 8 (`Invoke-Pester tests/scripts/ai-search/`) — all must pass.</step>
    <step order="10" name="Checkpoint (after test coverage + build)">Run `context-handoff` (silent: "✅ Checkpoint.").</step>
    <step order="11" name="Amend punch list annotation">EDIT `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` row A43 — add `last_known_status_after_execution` (target value: `applied — three-branch gate at Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1:340-366; unit+integration tests passing; A38 tag-scheme <finalized|placeholder> per Step 2`). Do NOT edit the row's numbered columns; append the annotation in the `last-known-status` cell per existing punch list convention (see A35 landing annotation for reference).</step>
    <step order="12" name="Report">Emit concise summary: gate applied (yes/no), unit+integration test count + pass/fail, A38 tag-scheme status (finalized vs placeholder), any Az.Accounts fallback taken (`Get-AzAccessToken` vs `az account get-access-token`), escalation-trigger firings (if any), files touched. Do NOT commit — main session handles commit after review.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger name="get-azaccesstoken-unsupported">If `Get-AzAccessToken -ResourceUrl "https://search.azure.com/"` is not supported by the installed Az.Accounts cmdlet version AND the `az account get-access-token --resource https://search.azure.com/` CLI fallback ALSO fails (e.g., token acquisition returns 401 or the AAD audience is rejected by the search plane), STOP — verify AAD auth path is actually supported for this AI Search service before landing the gate. May require alternative (e.g., `Search Index Data Contributor` role assignment verification, or a token-source that the AI Search REST plane accepts). Do NOT land the gate with a broken branch 2.</trigger>
    <trigger name="a38-tag-scheme-undefined">If A38's KV-tag key/value scheme for the secret-free marker is NOT yet finalized at execution time (A38 authoring may still be in-flight per remediation plan §7 S2 lane), coordinate: land the gate with env-config `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true` as the PRIMARY gate + KV-tag as SECONDARY with `# TODO(A38): finalize tag key/value` placeholder. Do NOT invent a divergent tag scheme (would force reconciliation at A38 landing time and undo A43's fleet-consistency guarantee).</trigger>
    <trigger name="script-refactored-since-2026-08-25">If `Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` has been refactored since 2026-08-25 (verify by grep + `git log --oneline -- scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` before editing) — e.g., the `:340-366` fallback moved to a different line range, or the `:617-660` `-CutoverBffSettings` gate was rewritten — reconcile with the latest state before applying the gate. Do NOT blind-apply against stale line numbers.</trigger>
    <trigger name="silent-fallback-already-partially-gated">If Step 1 grep reveals a partial pre-existing gate (e.g., someone added a marker check but not the AAD-token branch), STOP — this is either a prior in-flight A43 attempt (dedupe) or an unauthorized silent-partial-fix (audit). Report before proceeding.</trigger>
    <trigger name="tests-unavailable">If no PowerShell test surface exists AND creating one requires infrastructure decisions beyond the row scope (e.g., Pester version, mocking harness), escalate rather than invent a divergent test surface.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Row A43 has `last_known_status_after_execution` annotated in `notes/auth-v4-integration-draft-punch-rows.md` (grep confirms the annotation string on the A43 row).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` contains a gate BEFORE the current fallback (grep for the inline comment block referencing "§10.5 trap 2" or "A43" AND the three-branch decision comment).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On secret-free envs (marker present + secret missing), gate branch 1 fires and script exits with a NEW exit code (6) + FAIL-LOUD message naming the marker + linking to A38 omit contract (unit test asserts).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On MI-enabled envs (`AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true`), gate branch 2 fires and script acquires AAD token via `Get-AzAccessToken -ResourceUrl "https://search.azure.com/"` (or `az account get-access-token` fallback); `$restHeaders` contains `Authorization: Bearer` (unit test asserts) and `az search admin-key show` is NEVER executed (grep-verify in test).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">On pre-migration envs (no marker + no MI flag), gate branch 3 fires and current fallback behavior at `:356-366` runs UNCHANGED (unit test asserts byte-identical behavior vs pre-edit baseline; backwards compat).</criterion>
